# Two things about this pattern, both learned the hard way.
#
# Bare `scripts/` matches a directory of that name at *any* depth, not just the
# one at the root -- which silently kept apps/visual-tests/scripts out of the
# repository, so CI ran a lint script that was not there. Hence the leading
# slash.
#
# And `/scripts/` excludes the *directory*, which git will not descend into, so
# the negations below could not re-include anything: `git add scripts` was
# refused, and the pre-commit hook aborts its whole run on a path git refuses --
# silently dropping the formatting it had just applied to every other file.
# `/scripts/*` excludes the contents instead, which leaves the negations working.
/scripts/*
!scripts/branding-allowlist.json
!scripts/check-branding.mjs
!scripts/check-branding.test.mjs
!scripts/community-billing-page.test.mjs
!scripts/community-modal.test.mjs
!scripts/generate-release-notes.mjs
!scripts/vr.mjs
!packages/i18n/scripts/
!.github/scripts/
!.github/scripts/release_metadata.py
!.github/scripts/release_notes.py
!.github/scripts/tests/
!.github/scripts/tests/test_release_metadata.py
!.github/scripts/tests/test_release_notes.py
!.github/scripts/tests/test_release_workflow.py
!charts/hangar/scripts/

# i18n auto-generated types (regenerated on every build)
packages/i18n/src/types/keys.generated.ts

# Local security notes (not for version control)
/security/
/sast/

# Workstation-local state and linked worktrees
/.local/
